==English==
[[File:Scallion.jpg|thumb]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|scullion}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|scalun}} (variant of Old French {{m|fro|eschaloigne}}), from a Proto-Romance derivation of {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|Ascalonius|}} (in ''{{m|la|caepa||onion}} Ascalonius'', "shallot"), from {{m|la|Ascalo||Ascalon}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|Ἀσκάλων||{{w|Ashkelon|Ascalon}}, an ancient Palestinian port}}, from {{etyl|phn|en}} {{rfscript|phn|sc=Phnx}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈskæ.lɪ.ən]|[ˈskæ.ljn̩]|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{label|en|now|chiefly|US}} A [[spring onion]], ''[[Allium fistulosum]]''.
# {{label|en|now|chiefly|US}} Any of various similar members of the [[genus]] ''[[Allium]]''.
# Any onion that lacks a fully developed [[bulb]].
# {{label|en|US|Scotland}} A [[leek]].

====Synonyms====
{{checksense}}
* {{l|en|spring onion}}
* {{l|en|green onion}}

